## README.md Verification Tool Patterns

The README.md verification is a critical step before any file operations in the 1000xbrain cognitive architecture. Use these standardized tool call patterns to ensure proper README.md verification:

### 1. Standard README.md Verification Pattern

```typescript
// ALWAYS verify README.md before any file operations
// Step 1: Check directory README.md
read_file("1000xbrain/[target_directory]/README.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Step 2: For knowledge files, verify USE WHEN header requirement
grep_search("^# USE WHEN", false, "1000xbrain/knowledge/[target_subdirectory]/[target_file].md")

// Step 3: Only after verification, proceed with file operations
edit_file("1000xbrain/[target_directory]/[target_file].md", "Edit file with proper requirements")
```

### 2. Knowledge File Creation Pattern

```typescript
// ALWAYS follow this pattern when creating or modifying knowledge files
// Step 1: Check knowledge directory README.md
read_file("1000xbrain/knowledge/README.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Step 2: Check specific subdirectory README.md
read_file("1000xbrain/knowledge/[subdirectory]/README.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Step 3: Create file with proper USE WHEN header
edit_file("1000xbrain/knowledge/[subdirectory]/[new_file].md", 
          "Create new knowledge file with USE WHEN header",
          "# USE WHEN implementing [specific task], working with [related domain], or enhancing [related technology]\n\n# [Title]\n\n## File Purpose and Relationship\n\nThis file provides...\n\n## [Next Section]\n\n...")
```

### 3. README.md Validation Pattern

```typescript
// For comprehensive README.md validation:
// Step 1: Check for README.md files in all directories
grep_search("README\\.md$", false, "1000xbrain/*")

// Step 2: Validate USE WHEN headers in knowledge files
grep_search("^# USE WHEN", false, "1000xbrain/knowledge/*/*.md")

// Step 3: Find files missing USE WHEN headers
grep_search("^# [^U]", false, "1000xbrain/knowledge/*/*.md")
```

### 4. README.md Access Verification Pattern

```typescript
// Verify README.md access patterns:
// Step 1: First read README.md
read_file("1000xbrain/[target_directory]/README.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Step 2: Document that you've checked README.md
// This comment MUST be included before any file operations
// Example: "Verified README.md requirements for [target_directory]"

// Step 3: Only then proceed with file operations
read_file("1000xbrain/[target_directory]/[target_file].md", should_read_entire_file=true)
edit_file("1000xbrain/[target_directory]/[target_file].md", "Edit file with requirements from README.md")
```

### 5. New Directory Creation Pattern

```typescript
// When creating a new directory:
// Step 1: Check parent directory README.md
read_file("1000xbrain/[parent_directory]/README.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Step 2: Create README.md first
edit_file("1000xbrain/[parent_directory]/[new_directory]/README.md",
          "Create README.md for new directory",
          "# [New Directory Name]\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis directory contains...\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **File Structure**: Files should...\n2. **Formatting**: Follow these formatting standards...\n3. **Special Headers**: Files require these headers...\n\n## Related Components\n\n- **[Related Component]**: Relationship description\n")

// Step 3: Only after creating README.md, create other files
edit_file("1000xbrain/[parent_directory]/[new_directory]/[new_file].md", "Create new file following README.md requirements")
```

For detailed README.md verification standards, see the [scanning-process.md](scanning-process.md#readme-md-verification-process) file.

